## Module Breakdown

### `apps/candidates/`
- Core domain: candidate CRUD, status machine, status history
- Signals: `candidate_status_changed` → triggers Celery notification task

### `apps/vacancies/`
- Vacancy CRUD + close action
- Recruiter is automatically set from JWT token in the view

### `apps/interviews/`
- Schedule interview (recruiter only)
- Evaluate interview with score 1–10 (interviewer only)

### `apps/analytics/`
- Read-only analytics endpoints:
  - `GET /funnel/` — count by status with conversion %
  - `GET /time-to-hire/` — avg seconds from NEW to HIRED
  - `GET /candidates-by-status/` — dict of all statuses with counts

### `apps/users/`
- Custom User model (email-based auth, no username)
- JWT login/refresh via simplejwt
- `GET /me/` endpoint

### `apps/notifications/`
- Celery tasks for sending emails on candidate status changes
- Channel system: configurable via `NOTIFICATION_CHANNELS` setting

### `core/`
- `exceptions.py`: `BaseAppError`, `NotFoundError`, `ConflictError`, `ValidationError`
- `permissions.py`: `IsRecruiter`, `IsInterviewer`, `IsAdmin`, `IsRecruiterOrAdmin`
- `pagination.py`: Standard page/limit pagination

